==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[lede#Etymology_1|lede]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|leod||people|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|leode|lēode|people|lang=ang}}, plural of {{term|leod|lēod|person, man|lang=ang}}, from {{proto|Germanic|liudiz|people|lang=en}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|(e)lewədh-|man, people|lang=en}}. Cognate with {{etyl|sco|-}} {{term|lede||people|lang=sco}}, {{etyl|fy|-}} {{term|lie||people|lang=fy}}, {{etyl|vls|-}} {{term|lieden||people|lang=vls}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|lui|lui(den)|people|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Leute||people|lang=de}}, {{etyl|no|-}} {{term|lyd||people|lang=no}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|lēd|lē-ōd}}, {{IPA|/liːd/|/liːod/}}, {{SAMPA|/li:d/|/li:od/}}
* {{homophones|lead}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|pl=leod|pl2=leods}}

# {{context|collectively|obsolete}} [[people|People]].
# {{obsolete}} A [[people]], [[nation]], people group.
# {{obsolete}} A [[man]], [[person]].

===Anagrams===
* [[dole#English|dole]], [[lode#English|lode]], [[olde#English|olde]], [[OLED#English|OLED]]

